+<a id="m158"></a>
+### M158 — No accountability recommendation on uncertain January passage is not general exoneration
+
+**Original ID:** CL006. **Type:** Source-scope qualification and distinct affirmative failure findings.
+
+CIA physical pp.105–106 / printed pp.80–81 makes no accountability recommendation concerning January informal passage because it could neither confirm nor refute that passage. The same discussion reports a separate March 2000 failure to tell the FBI about Hazmi's US-bound departure and later missed opportunities. Page105 also recommends an Accountability Board assessment of systemic watchlisting management.
+
+- Uncertainty about one delivery issue is retained alongside affirmative findings on other failures; it is not recast as proof all conduct was proper.
+- The report's findings are not the final disposition of a later Accountability Board, discipline decision, criminal inquiry or historical-cause adjudication. Those later outcomes were not established in this pass.
+- DOJ's own accountability assessment distinguishes CIA responsibility, FBI detailee initiative and inadequate further follow-up. Those statements do not identify a single attack-motivated actor.
+- DOJ IV.D's introductory assessment says none of the evaluated FBI employees committed misconduct, although several performed below what they should have. It expressly leaves CIA personnel accountability to CIA OIG. Preserve that adverse-to-misconduct finding with the performance criticisms; do not extend it to every CIA action.
+
+**Exact source locations and retained excerpts:** [review section](../../broader-evidence/cia-lead-verification-2026-10-26/REPORT.md#cl006); report SHA-256 `90f2d4ef20741ee1e1b0b6ac8f24b668d501115470a75b66a30dff21559e9fd9`. Primary PDF physical/printed pages, HTML sections and text blocks are retained in register.json.
+
+**Public source links:** [source 1](https://documents.theblackvault.com/documents/cia/DOC_0006184107.pdf) · [source 2](https://oig.justice.gov/sites/default/files/archive/special/0506/chapter5.htm).
+
+**Next record/test:** Obtain the underlying March cables/access audits, action logs and the issue-specific accountability referral/response and final board or management dispositions. Do not infer an actual sanction from a recommendation.
+
+**Limit:** Supports an accountability inquiry, not a final finding of conspiracy, exoneration, criminal intent or WTC 7 involvement.
+
+**Related / overlapping:** [M153](#m153), [M154](#m154), [M157](#m157).
